<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S3-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S3-002" ;
  triage:title "Windows reload path entirely absent — _reload param discarded, SIGBREAK not registered (lifecycle_control.rs:188-219)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/lifecycle_control.rs:188-219 — the Windows lifecycle registration function takes a _reload: &Arc<AtomicBool> parameter with underscore prefix (explicitly discarded). SIGBREAK/CTRL_BREAK_EVENT is not registered. Sprint-S3.md AC (line 99) requires Windows provides real lifecycle-control behavior for both shutdown AND reload. ADR-daemon/architecture.md §3.1.3 maps SIGBREAK/CTRL_BREAK_EVENT → bounded reload/rescan. REQ-DAEMON-SIGNAL-001 (requirements.md:176-181) requires this mapping. Fix together with ATM-QA-S3-001 (CI-BLOCK-001-S3): use signal_hook::flag::register for both SIGINT (terminate) and SIGBREAK (reload); rename _reload → reload; call state_change.notify() after setting reload flag. (quality-mgr reported as WIN-RELOAD-001 in S.3 QA-2 report.)" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
